## Layer 2 -- Jest live-render VTs (isolated primitives)

For shared primitives in `@leo/design-system/src/primitives/` and for
small leaf components that do not hit the network, do mount them with
React Testing Library and assert real behaviour.

### When to use

- A primitive in `@leo/design-system` exposes interactive props
  (`SegmentedTabs.onChange`, `ToolbarActions.onClick`,
  `ConfirmDialog` flow).
- A leaf UI component has branching logic that benefits from running
  the actual code path (form validation, computed labels).

### What to use

- `@testing-library/react` for mounting.
- `@testing-library/user-event` for interaction (NOT `fireEvent`).
- `jest.config.js` already maps `@leo/design-system` to the workspace
  source, so imports work without a build step.

### What NOT to do

Do NOT live-render a full page that calls `api.get()` on mount. Stub
the API and assert via static-source instead -- the maintenance cost
of stubs across 8+ pages outweighs the benefit.

