## Layer 3 -- Playwright user journeys + axe-core

Playwright lives in `services/ui/e2e/`. Every designed user journey
MUST have a spec file. The Wave E Phase 7 work also requires every
Knowledge tab body to ship a Playwright screenshot test that pins
the new layout.

### Required journey coverage

- `dashboard.spec.ts` -- role-first dashboard for each role.
- `pipeline.spec.ts` -- end-to-end coding pipeline.
- `review-workflow.spec.ts` -- coding review queue.
- `report-builder.spec.ts` -- report assembly.
- `episode-timeline.spec.ts` -- patient pathway view.
- `patient-workflow.spec.ts` -- full patient journey.
- `encounters-batch.spec.ts` -- batch processing.

### Accessibility (axe-core)

`a11y-baseline.spec.ts` runs `@axe-core/playwright` against every
shipped page. Every page / wizard step MUST pass axe-core with ZERO
critical or serious violations. WCAG 2.1 AA is the bar.

```ts
import AxeBuilder from "@axe-core/playwright";

const results = await new AxeBuilder({ page })
  .withTags(["wcag2a", "wcag2aa", "wcag21a", "wcag21aa"])
  .analyze();
expect(results.violations.filter(v =>
  ["critical", "serious"].includes(v.impact ?? "")
)).toEqual([]);
```

### CSS-alerts spec

`css-alerts.spec.ts` enforces visual regressions on the role-first
shell. Run it before merging any change to `RoleShellProvider.tsx`,
the navigation, or the top-level layout.

