## Definition of done for any UI change

A Class B UI change is NOT done until ALL of the following are true:

1. The DI lists `verification.test_protocol: "VT-LEO-AI-<N>"` and
   that VT YAML exists and is consistent with the test file.
2. The VT YAML's `metadata.test_file_paths` lists the actual jest
   spec(s).
3. `npx jest --testPathPatterns "<spec-name>" --no-coverage` is
   green locally.
4. The full Wave E regression sweep is green:
   ```bash
   cd services/ui && npx jest --no-coverage \
     --testPathPatterns "knowledge-tab|chrome|theme-port|wave-d|design-system-primitives|training-data"
   ```
5. The VT YAML's `execution_history` records the run with
   `result: "pass"` and `status` is set to `"passed"`.
6. For any new visible surface, the corresponding Playwright spec is
   updated AND `a11y-baseline.spec.ts` still passes.
7. The traceability matrices (`DC-TM-001-traceability-matrix.md`,
   `DC-TM-002-traceability-matrix.csv`) and `design-controls/README.md`
   are updated with the new DI / DO / Risk / VT rows.

